  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural Markets, Value Addition and Trade Development Project (AMVAT) in Juba County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cordaid as one of the implementing partners for the Agricultural Markets, Value Addition and Trade Development Project (AMVAT) in Juba County. The project will provide much needed skills and inputs for farmers to increase productivity, aggregation capacity and post-harvest agro-processing equipment to improve value addition. The Agricultural Markets, Value Addition and Trade Development Project (AMVAT) uses an agricultural value chain approach with emphasis on the development of producer associations. It will also provide capacity building to improve the marketing and trade environment for agricultural products to increase incomes and create jobs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data will be disaggregated by gender - female-headed household, male-headed household, and child headed households
The project will provide inclusive and adaptive programming that will benefit men,women and young people of all social construct of age,gender and religion,race,colour etc</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective is to increase agricultural productivity and value addition-The intervention will contribute to 1. &#x201C;Sustainable increase in agricultural production and productivity&#x201D; and 2. &#x2018;&#x2019;Agriculture-based economic growth and incomes increased&#x2019;&#x2019;The Overall project objective is to contribute to reduced food insecurity and malnutrition, poverty reduction and building of community and household resilience in Juba County 

The project Outcome is to contribute to Reduced Food Insecurity, Poverty Reduction and Building of Community and households&#x2019; resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
